# Shell scripts must keep LF endings so shebangs stay executable under core.autocrlf=true
*.sh text eol=lf
# Python scripts for the same reason: under core.autocrlf=true a fresh checkout would otherwise
# materialize .github/scripts/tests/fixture-feed.py with CRLF. Harmless while the harness invokes
# it as `python3 fixture-feed.py`, and a broken shebang the moment the stub is made executable.
*.py text eol=lf
# Nuspec fixtures are byte-identical copies of published package manifests (incl. a UTF-8 BOM);
# they exist to prove the guard's parser against a real-world document, so no line-ending
# conversion may ever be applied in either direction.
*.nuspec -text
